[info] - every record's schema version is its current SchemaVersions constant
[info] - absent options are JSON null and enums are their case names
[info] - an unknown enum value is rejected
[info] - evidence-v1 EvidenceType names are frozen; only TEXT_CHUNK and PROFILE are semantic
[info] - the Phase 9 evidence types round-trip as evidence-v1 and are graph evidence only
[info] - malformed JSON is rejected, not thrown
[info] ConfigLoaderSpec:
[info] - the reference file alone loads as a valid local configuration
[info] - default graph windows are the three D-10 windows
[info] - one bucket per environment with the eight ruling-7 prefixes
[info] - a layer that still sets a removed per-purpose bucket key is rejected
[info] - precedence: the config file overrides the reference
[info] - precedence: environment variables override the config file and the reference
[info] - unlisted environment variables are ignored
[info] - an invalid bucket name or malformed or duplicate prefix is rejected
[info] - every documented environment variable maps to a path in the reference
[info] - a missing config file is an error, not a silent fallback
[info] - a non-local environment must replace every placeholder
[info] - a non-local environment with every value supplied loads
[info] - M10: table prefix and Neptune loader role ARN are keys with env overrides
[info] - M10: malformed prefixes and ARNs are rejected; placeholders are rejected outside local
[info] - Phase 9: planner and synthesis models default to Haiku 4.5 and are env-overridable
[info] - Phase 9: runtime, ranking, and graph-read defaults (RUNTIME.md section 20)
[info] - Phase 9: runtime bounds and cross-key checks are enforced
[info] - every runtime and graph-read leaf in the reference is read by the loader
[info] - entity-resolution thresholds must be ordered within [0, 1]
[info] - entity-resolution policy version defaults to er-v2 and is env-overridable
[info] - entity-resolution block and conflict-group limits: defaults, env overrides, positive
[info] - a window whose start year exceeds its end year is rejected
[info] - an unsupported config version is rejected
[info] EvaluationSpec:
[info] - hand-computed metrics: precision, recall, F1, coverage, unresolved rate, confusion matrix
[info] - metrics by match path, and undefined rates are None
[info] - threshold sensitivity moves only score-decided rows
[info] - error lists: false positives, then false negatives with rejections before abstentions
[info] - join checks traceability to the key file and label values
[info] - rows are scored on the key file's decision and path, not on the stratum they were sampled in
[info] - the reported policy version comes from the key file, which must name exactly one
[info] - the evaluator refuses a labels file outside a labels/ directory
[info] - leakage check: only the evaluator mentions labels/ among main sources
[info] AdjudicationSpec:
[info] - a schema-valid reply is accepted and carries prompt and model versions
[info] - schema validation rejects every malformed, fabricated, or out-of-schema reply
[info] - a fabricated identifier becomes ABSTAIN after the bounded retry
[info] - malformed JSON is retried once; a valid second reply is used
[info] - the model may abstain, and abstention keeps the pair UNRESOLVED
[info] - prompt injection in a title stays inside the data block and cannot close the delimiter
[info] - cache: hits skip the client and the budget; only schema-valid replies are cached
[info] - cache keys depend on input hash, prompt version, model version, and policy version
[info] - JSONL file cache persists entries across instances
[info] - budget: no call beyond the maximum adjudications or the token budget
[info] - prompt and schema resources load, and the schema's reason codes match the validator
[info] AdjudicateSampleSpec:
[info] - select is a seeded sample of LLM-band decisions only, independent of input order
[info] - sessions are bounded by --max and resume from the cache without repeating calls
[info] - the source decision is unchanged; ABSTAIN keeps the pair UNRESOLVED
[info] - a client error after its retry halts the session; the rest stay pending
[info] - live mode requires --live and --profile before any input is read
[info] - an expired token refreshes the credentials and retries once, through the throttle
[info] - a second expired token or any other error is not retried again
[info] - RefreshingCredentials resolves through a delegate rebuilt after refresh
